15 0 obj
<< /A 38 0 R /Alt (PRISMA flow diagram illustrating study identification and selection process for a systematic review. Two thousand seventy-eight records identified from several databases, ninety-nine duplicates removed, one thousand nine hundred seventy-nine screened, ten sought for retrieval, with one not retrieved and one excluded for missing key outcome data, resulting in eight studies included.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 29 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 39 0 R /Alt (Forest plot graphic showing meta-analysis results for mean change in femoral venous blood flow velocity across different frequencies of intervention, with separate panels for 3, 5, 6, 10, 12, and 15 cycles per minute. Each panel displays study authors, effect sizes with ninety-five percent confidence intervals, study weights, and pooled estimates using random-effects REML models. Results indicate increasing effect sizes with higher cycles per minute and heterogeneity statistics are reported for each frequency group.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 40 0 R /Alt (Forest plot graphic showing meta-analysis of mean change in femoral venous blood flow velocity at three frequencies: 20, 30, and 40 cycles per minute. Each section lists individual study results with effect sizes and confidence intervals, overall pooled estimates as green diamonds, and heterogeneity statistics. Horizontal axes represent blood flow velocity in centimeters per second.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 41 0 R /Alt (Forest plots summarizing meta-analysis of mean change in femoral venous blood flow velocity, measured in centimeters per second, at 60, 80, and 100 cycles per minute. Each panel shows studies with effect sizes and confidence intervals as blue squares and lines. The pooled effect size, shown as a green diamond, is 9.74 cm/s at 60 cycles/min, 11.37 cm/s at 80 cycles/min, and 9.00 cm/s at 100 cycles/min, with details regarding heterogeneity and statistical significance for each group.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
